================================================================================
                     MULTIVERSE CONNECTION REQUIREMENT
================================================================================

Any world or simulation created with the AO World Engine that wishes to be
recognized as part of the official RE:ECHO multiverse MUST:

1. REGISTER WITH LAYER REGISTRY - Connect to the Layer Registry AO process
2. ENABLE ECHO PROPAGATION - Allow cross-layer echo bleed events
3. RESPECT GEO-CLAIMS - Do not claim coordinates already claimed by another layer
4. SHARE CODEC COMPATIBILITY - Use compatible data formats for interoperability

This requirement ensures:
- Echoes can travel between all connected worlds
- GeoEchoes app can discover content from any layer
- Users experience a unified, interconnected multiverse

Forks may modify the engine freely under AGPL-3.0, but only deployments
registered with the Layer Registry are considered part of the official
RE:ECHO multiverse network.

For Layer Registry process ID and connection details, see:
https://github.com/WandernGeo/ao-world-engine/docs/MULTIVERSE_ARCHITECTURE.md

